lpwm_swm — attribution
======================

This subpackage (the LpWM Piecewise / OGBench-Cube experiments) is built on and
depends on **stable-worldmodel**, an MIT-licensed library by the GalilAI-group:

    stable-worldmodel
    Copyright (c) 2026 GalilAI-group
    https://github.com/galilai-group/stable-worldmodel
    Licensed under the MIT License.

It also follows and ports code from **le-wm** (Lucas Maes) — the LpWM neural-module,
loss, and predictor code here is adapted from it:

    le-wm
    Copyright (c) 2026 Lucas Maes
    https://github.com/lucas-maes/le-wm
    Licensed under the MIT License.

What is used from stable-worldmodel (imported as a dependency, not vendored):
  - the training/eval/planning infrastructure (World, EnvPool, WorldModelPolicy,
    the planning ShootingCostEvaluator + Objective + solvers, the dataset/format
    registry) and the `stable_pretraining` training loop;
  - the **Piecewise** (`swm/Piecewise-v0`) and **OGBench-Cube** (`swm/OGBCube-v0`)
    environments, which are upstream stable-worldmodel components (unmodified).

What is original to this subpackage (the LpWM method):
  - the `LpWM` world model (`model.py`), the sparse `RepReLU` link and the
    predictor/projector blocks (`module.py`), and the `RDMReg`
    regularizer (`loss.py`);
  - the training/eval entry points and Hydra configs.

The neural-module and loss code here is ported from the LpWM stable-worldmodel
fork and re-wired to the public stable-worldmodel `Dynamics` / planning API.

This subpackage is released under the same MIT license as the rest of this
repository (see the top-level LICENSE). The full MIT copyright and permission
notices for le-wm and stable-worldmodel are reproduced in the top-level NOTICE.
